From 3cfa0e92f86359bb99e87691956bb9d1d77e6ae0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kob <kob@invalid>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:00:13 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Cache workload above downloads; imports and warming choose
 their workload

Workload::Cache is stream-side background work (a client caching a stream ahead,
imports for a stream). Downloads serve background waiters by rank: Cache, Queue,
Warm, Health. A Cache request runs in its reader's own lane, and while one waits
for a connection, lower-ranked work takes none, so connections drain to it
instead of pipelining downloads forever. Rules::workload sets an import's
workload (Queue by default). Reader::with_warming warms archive members and
encrypted files on the Warm workload, not Health. A retired pool's connections
log out and wait for the provider to close before freeing their account permit.
